<item>
<title>Useful metrics. Not the point.</title>
<link>https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/field-notes/useful-metrics-not-the-point.html</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/field-notes/useful-metrics-not-the-point.html</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
<description>Attendance, completion, certification and a great feedback score prove the training happened. They don’t show whether people use what they learned.</description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/2026-09-30-useful-metrics-not-the-point.jpg" alt="Slide on a red background. A training evaluation form lists attendance, completion, certification and a 4.8/5 feedback score, all ticked. A red stamp across it reads: Useful metrics. Not the point. Below: They measure the room. Not what happens Monday. A good training program builds real capability. Enablement turns capability into action. And action is where adoption begins. Especially with AI."></p>]]></content:encoded>
</item>
<item>
<title>You bought the AI tools. Now what?</title>
<link>https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/field-notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools.html</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/field-notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools.html</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
<description>Eight lessons on getting people to actually use the AI tools their company already paid for.</description>
<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/01.jpg" alt="Slide 1 of 12. 8 LESSONS. You bought the AI tools. Now how do you get people to actually use them?"></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/02.jpg" alt="Slide 2 of 12. THE REAL MOMENT. Adoption isn&#x27;t about writing a clever prompt. It&#x27;s someone on a Tuesday morning, looking at the work in front of them, and thinking: “I could use AI for this.” I&#x27;ve spent 20+ years as a writer and trainer. The gap between AI access and AI adoption is where people like us can help."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/03.jpg" alt="Slide 3 of 12. LESSON 01. 01. Start with the annoying work. Skip the AI at first. Start with the employee. Ask: What takes too long? What do you keep rewriting? Which report do you dread every Thursday? 45 → 10 min with AI. Turning meeting notes into actions. People adopt tools that remove friction."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/04.jpg" alt="Slide 4 of 12. LESSON 02. 02. Say it in normal language. Most employees don&#x27;t need a lesson on large language models. They need to know what AI can do for them before lunch. AI can support knowledge synthesis. → Give it three documents. Ask what changed. Use generative AI to improve content. → Give it your rough email. Ask it to make it clearer without changing your meaning."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/05.jpg" alt="Slide 5 of 12. LESSON 03. 03. Treat AI like a very fast new colleague. Reads hundreds of pages in seconds. Knows nothing about your situation unless you explain it. YOU SAY. “Make this better.” You get… anything. YOU SAY. “For senior management. Under 200 words. Focus on the three risks. Plain language.” You get what you need. That&#x27;s prompting. Not magic words. Just better instructions."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/06.jpg" alt="Slide 6 of 12. LESSON 04. 04. Train on their work, not demo work. A generic demo impresses for five minutes. Then everyone goes back to their desk. Project managers. STATUS REPORTS · MEETING NOTES · ACTION TRACKERS. HR. JOB DESCRIPTIONS · POLICIES · EMPLOYEE COMMS. Operations. SOPS · REPORTS · RECURRING TASKS. People need to see themselves in the training."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/07.jpg" alt="Slide 7 of 12. LESSON 05. 05. Remove the fear. The biggest barrier usually isn&#x27;t capability. It&#x27;s uncertainty. Can I upload this? Can I use customer data? What if it&#x27;s wrong? Am I even allowed? Can I send what it writes? What&#x27;s safe. What&#x27;s not. What needs checking. Where humans decide. People experiment more when they know where the guardrails are."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/08.jpg" alt="Slide 8 of 12. LESSON 06. 06. Make the first win small. No huge transformation program needed. Sometimes it starts with: “Turn these messy notes into five to-dos.” “Summarize this 30-page doc before my meeting.” “Give me a first draft so I&#x27;m not staring at a blank page.” Ten minutes saved leads to the next question: “What else can I use this for?”"></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/09.jpg" alt="Slide 9 of 12. LESSON 07. 07. Recipes, not a cookbook. “100 AI Prompts” Most people open it once. AI FOR PROJECT MANAGERS. 1. Turn meeting notes into actions. 2. Draft the weekly status update. 3. Compare two versions of a document. 4. Summarize project risks. 5. Prep questions for a stakeholder meeting. Five things a team will actually use beat a hundred they won&#x27;t."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/10.jpg" alt="Slide 10 of 12. LESSON 08. 08. Training ≠ adoption. 100 attendees ≠ 100 AI users. Attendance is easy to measure. Behavior is harder. TWO WEEKS LATER, ASK. Are people still using it? For which tasks? Where are they getting stuck? What have they stopped doing manually? Adoption sounds like: “This is how I work now.”"></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/11.jpg" alt="Slide 11 of 12. THE TAKEAWAY. Why writers and trainers matter in AI adoption. AI may be the technology. Adoption is still a human problem. WE ALREADY KNOW HOW TO. Understand an audience. Make complicated things less intimidating. Build examples and learning journeys. Explain without making anyone feel stupid."></p><p><img src="https://neowriter.github.io/portfolio/notes/you-bought-the-ai-tools/12.jpg" alt="Slide 12 of 12. SO, ONE QUESTION. “What can AI do?” What could AI make easier for you today?"></p>]]></content:encoded>
